{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/pulls/2853","id":4053540861,"node_id":"PR_kwDON8_yq87xnB_9","html_url":"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/pull/2853","diff_url":"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/pull/2853.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/pull/2853.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2853","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/pulls/2853/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/pulls/2853/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2853/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/statuses/b8a81c099d0d30607416211f819db8a40bda5371","number":2853,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"specs: add compliance-fields extension — tax/audit record + verifier disqualification rules (#2848)","user":{"login":"wowlegend","id":36414223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDE0MjIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36414223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend","html_url":"https://github.com/wowlegend","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Spec for the `compliance-fields` extension proposed in #2848 (issue-first per specs/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\nAn optional, signed compliance record composing with `offer-receipt` by digest reference — never touching its EIP-712 types. Summary of what's normative:\n\n- **Tiers are legal thresholds:** MINIMAL is isomorphic to the EU simplified-invoice content (VAT Directive Art 226b); whether it suffices as an invoice is decided by the invoicing rules that apply to the supply (Art 219a). FULL aligns to EN 16931. Tiers MUST NOT be mapped onto verification-confidence scales.\n- **VAT treatment:** an optional EN 16931 VAT category (BT-118) with an exemption reason (BT-121/BT-120), required, forbidden or fixed per category after EN 16931 BR-*-10 and the VATEX list (for AE/K/G/O the VATEX code is required, where EN 16931 also accepts a text), an optional `buyer.taxIdBasis` (`verified`/`declared`/`none`, present only with a non-empty `buyer.taxId`) stating the basis on which the issuer treated the buyer's tax ID, and an optional `buyer.declarationDigest` (present only with the basis) carrying the digest of a declaration the buyer supplied and the issuer relied on: keccak256 over its exact bytes, as 66-character lowercase `0x` hex; the declaration's format is outside the extension. `seq` and the buyer's name and address are M where the invoicing rules that apply to the supply require them, as they do for every full invoice, and the buyer's tax ID where those rules require it, as Art 226(4) does on a full invoice where the buyer is liable for the VAT or the supply is an intra-Community supply of goods. Every supply Arts 220a(2)/238(3) bar from a simplified invoice needs a full invoice; no rule in the extension requires these members because of a supply's VAT category or amount. Party members can be personal data: the invoicing rules that apply decide which of them a record must carry, whether an issuer may include others is for the law that governs its processing of them, not for this extension, and attestation signs digests only.\n- **Canonicalization v1 = RFC 8785 (JCS)**, digest = keccak256, versioned **together** via `canonicalizationVersion` (changing either independently invalidates existing signatures). Byte-level conformance vectors are inline in the spec — including the integer-like-key ordering case that sort-then-stringify implementations get wrong.\n- **Corrective chain:** `refundOf` + the ACP/UCP adjustment vocabulary, per ViDA's corrective-invoice reference; composes with `exact`, `auth-capture`, and `batch-settlement` refund flows.\n- **Sequential numbering:** `seq`/`correctionSeq` carry Art 226(2)/BT-1 semantics, assigned by the issuer before the record is attested. From the records it holds, a verifier can establish their order but not their completeness. A sequence attested only by the issuer, or by a party that issues or numbers the records on its behalf, evidences ordering only; verifiers MUST NOT treat it as evidence that no record was omitted, or that no other record carries the same `seq` and `correctionSeq`. Who supplies non-issuer observation is service-layer, out of scope.\n- **Independence:** a record attested only by the transaction's parties or their delegates (parties that sign, issue or number records on their behalf; an attestor that signs in its own name is not a delegate merely because a party engaged or paid it, or supplied the records it signs) MUST NOT be treated as an independent or neutral finding.\n- Deliberately out of scope: tax computation and VAT determination, verification of tax identifiers, filing/transmission channels, delivery proof (complementary to #1195 SAR and #2833 delivery-receipt — either's digest can ride along), identity.\n\nThe spec is self-contained: every verifier-reject rule in it applies from its text alone. The inline vectors test canonicalization conformance, and the verifier-reject rules added in this revision carry two-sided examples. Happy to iterate on placement/naming per maintainer preference.\n\nDisclosure: the majority of this PR was generated with AI tools.\n","labels":[{"id":9941168930,"node_id":"LA_kwDON8_yq88AAAACUIozIg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/x402-foundation/x402/labels/specs","name":"specs","description":"Spec changes or additions","color":"15a8f6","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-14T15:03:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T15:58:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"dde88dedd36d6a97db10deb8d6fdbfbb1827777a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"wowlegend:compliance-fields-extension","ref":"compliance-fields-extension","repo":{"id":1300573478,"node_id":"R_kgDOTYUtJg","name":"x402","full_name":"wowlegend/x402","owner":{"login":"wowlegend","id":36414223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDE0MjIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36414223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend","html_url":"https://github.com/wowlegend","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wowlegend/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"A payments protocol for the internet. Built on HTTP.","homepage":"https://x402.org","language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":false,"top